posix: Fix double-free after allocation failure in regcomp

The regcomp function in the GNU C Library versions from 2.4 to 2.44 is
subject to a double free / use-after-free if some previous allocation
fails.  When one of the arrays growing the internal NFA node table
(re_dfa_add_node) or the bracket range table (build_range_exp) is
reallocated to a new address but a subsequent reallocation of a paired
array fails, the stale pointers to the blocks already released by
realloc are left in place and freed again during cleanup.  The failure
can be triggered by a malloc failure or by using an interposed malloc
that injects random malloc failures.  The double free can allow buffer
manipulation depending on how the regex is constructed.  This issue
affects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C Library.

This is a sibling of CVE-2025-8058 (GLIBC-SA-2025-0005), whose fix
addressed the bracket-expression parsing path only.

